# Testing Patterns

## Pytest
- Name: `test_<fn>_<scenario>_<expected>`; plain `assert`; fixtures over `setUp`
- Parametrize multi-input cases; shared fixtures in nearest `conftest.py`
- Mock time/random/network/LLM — never hit real LLM APIs in unit tests

## Quality
- Deterministic and isolated; unit tests under 100ms; prefer behavior over internals
- Cover happy path **and** failure/edge cases (null, empty, boundaries)
- Aim ~80%+ coverage on domain logic; pin seeds for ML (`random_state` / `np.random.seed`)

## This repo
- Harness/hook tests live under `tests/eval/`; run `make eval-fast` for local gates
- Prefer integration-style hook tests over pure mocks when behavior is shell I/O
